---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = '8 September 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Real product collects, uses and protects personal data across this website and its professional services."
  noindex
>
  <section class="wrap page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Real product / Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">Last updated: {updated}</p>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="prose legal">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how Real Product collects, uses and
        protects personal data when you use this website, submit a Reality Check
        request, contact us or engage our professional services.
      </p>
      <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
      <p>The data controller is:</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Víctor Andújar Murcia</strong><br />NIF: <strong
          >53296659R</strong
        ><br />Trading as: <strong>Real Product</strong><br />Avinguda Comte
        Ramon Berenguer 146, Baixos 2a<br />08690 Santa Coloma de Cervelló,
        Barcelona, Spain<br />Email: <strong
          ><a href="mailto:victorandujarmurcia@gmail.com"
            >victorandujarmurcia@gmail.com</a
          ></strong>
      </p>
      <h2>2. Applicable Law</h2>
      <p>
        Personal data is processed in accordance with applicable data-protection
        legislation, including:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (General Data Protection Regulation &mdash;
          GDPR).
        </li><li>
          Spanish Organic Law 3/2018 on Personal Data Protection and Guarantee
          of Digital Rights (LOPDGDD).
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>3. Personal Data We Collect</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on how you interact with Real Product, we may collect
        information such as:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name.</li><li>Email address.</li><li>
          Company or project information.
        </li><li>Product or website URL.</li><li>
          Information you provide about your product.
        </li><li>Repository URL where voluntarily provided.</li><li>
          Messages and communications exchanged with Real Product.
        </li><li>
          Information necessary to prepare proposals, provide services or issue
          invoices.
        </li><li>
          Technical information generated when interacting with the website
          where necessary for its operation and security.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If a professional engagement requires access to repositories or
        technical systems, additional information may be temporarily accessible
        as necessary to provide the agreed services.
      </p>
      <h2>4. Reality Check Requests</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit a Reality Check request, the information you provide is
        used to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Review your request.</li><li>
          Understand your product and technical context.
        </li><li>Determine whether Real Product can assist you.</li><li>
          Perform or prepare the requested assessment.
        </li><li>Contact you regarding your request.</li><li>
          Propose further services where relevant to your request.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Submitting a Reality Check does not automatically subscribe you to
        marketing communications.
      </p>
      <h2>5. Purposes and Legal Bases</h2>
      <p>Personal data may be processed for the following purposes:</p>
      <p><strong>Responding to enquiries and Reality Check requests</strong></p>
      <p>
        Data is processed in order to respond to actions initiated by you and,
        where applicable, to take steps at your request before entering into a
        contract.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR and, where appropriate, Real
        Product's legitimate interest in responding to professional enquiries
        under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Providing professional services</strong></p>
      <p>
        Where you engage Real Product, personal data is processed as necessary
        to manage and perform the contractual relationship.
      </p>
      <p>The legal basis is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR.</p>
      <p><strong>Billing, accounting and legal obligations</strong></p>
      <p>
        Certain information may be processed and retained to comply with tax,
        accounting and other legal obligations.
      </p>
      <p>The legal basis is Article 6(1)(c) GDPR.</p>
      <p><strong>Website security and prevention of abuse</strong></p>
      <p>
        Limited technical information may be processed where necessary to
        protect the website, prevent abuse, diagnose technical issues and
        maintain the security of the service.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis is Real Product's legitimate interest under Article
        6(1)(f) GDPR.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Marketing communications</strong></p>
      <p>
        Real Product will not use information submitted through a Reality Check
        request to send unrelated promotional communications unless there is an
        appropriate legal basis to do so.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where consent is required, such communications will only be sent after
        obtaining that consent and it may be withdrawn at any time.
      </p>
      <h2>6. Data Minimisation</h2>
      <p>
        Real Product aims to collect only information reasonably necessary for
        the relevant purpose.
      </p>
      <p>
        Please do not submit passwords, API keys, private credentials, sensitive
        personal information or unnecessary personal data through general
        website forms.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where credentials or privileged access are required for professional
        work, a more appropriate and secure method should be used.
      </p>
      <h2>7. Source Code and Repository Access</h2>
      <p>
        Providing a repository URL does not necessarily grant Real Product
        access to private source code.
      </p>
      <p>
        If repository access is required for an assessment or paid engagement,
        access may be requested separately.
      </p>
      <p>
        Information accessed within private repositories will be used solely for
        the relevant assessment or professional engagement and will not be
        intentionally disclosed or reused for unrelated purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Clients are encouraged to provide the minimum permissions necessary and
        to revoke access when it is no longer required.
      </p>
      <h2>8. How Long We Keep Data</h2>
      <p>
        Personal data is retained only for as long as reasonably necessary for
        the purpose for which it was collected.
      </p>
      <p>As a general principle:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Enquiries and unsuccessful project requests may be retained for a
          reasonable period to manage follow-up and maintain a record of
          communications.
        </li><li>
          Information relating to active clients is retained for the duration of
          the professional relationship.
        </li><li>
          Contractual, invoicing and accounting information may be retained for
          the periods required by applicable Spanish law.
        </li><li>
          Technical access credentials should not be retained beyond the period
          for which they are necessary.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Data may be retained for longer where necessary to establish, exercise
        or defend legal claims or comply with a legal obligation.
      </p>
      <h2>9. Service Providers</h2>
      <p>
        Real Product may use third-party providers necessary to operate the
        website and provide its services.
      </p>
      <p>These may include providers for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Website hosting and deployment.</li><li>
          Email delivery and communication.
        </li><li>Infrastructure and databases.</li><li>
          Development and repository hosting.
        </li><li>Analytics, if implemented.</li><li>
          Professional productivity and development tools.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Where these providers process personal data on behalf of Real Product,
        appropriate data-processing arrangements will be used where required by
        law.
      </p>
      <h2>10. International Data Transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Some technology providers may process data outside the European Economic
        Area.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where this occurs, Real Product will rely on a legally recognised
        transfer mechanism where required, such as:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>An adequacy decision adopted by the European Commission.</li><li>
          Standard Contractual Clauses.
        </li><li>Another valid safeguard recognised under the GDPR.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>11. Vercel</h2>
      <p>
        The Real Product website may use infrastructure provided by <strong
          >Vercel</strong
        > for hosting and deployment.
      </p>
      <p>
        As part of normal web infrastructure operation, technical information
        such as IP addresses, request metadata and security logs may be
        processed.
      </p>
      <p>
        The exact processing performed by infrastructure providers is governed
        by their applicable privacy and data-processing terms.
      </p>
      <h2>12. Email Services</h2>
      <p>
        Real Product may use external email infrastructure to receive or send
        transactional communications relating to requests and services.
      </p>
      <p>
        Information necessary to deliver these communications, such as email
        addresses and message content, may therefore be processed by the
        relevant email provider.
      </p>
      <h2>13. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Real Product aims to minimise the use of cookies and tracking
        technologies.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cookies that are strictly necessary for the technical operation or
        security of the website may be used without consent where permitted by
        law.
      </p>
      <p>
        If non-essential analytics, advertising or tracking technologies
        requiring consent are introduced, appropriate information and consent
        mechanisms will be implemented before those technologies are activated.
      </p>
      <h2>14. Automated Decision-Making</h2>
      <p>
        Real Product does not make decisions producing legal or similarly
        significant effects about users solely through automated processing.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI or automated tools may assist with technical workflows, but relevant
        professional decisions remain subject to human judgement.
      </p>
      <h2>15. Sharing Personal Data</h2>
      <p>Real Product does not sell personal data.</p>
      <p>Personal data may be shared only where reasonably necessary:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          With service providers supporting the operation of the website or
          professional services.
        </li><li>
          Where required by law, regulation or a competent authority.
        </li><li>
          Where necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims.
        </li><li>
          Where you have expressly requested or authorised the disclosure.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>16. Your Data Protection Rights</h2>
      <p>Under the GDPR, you may have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Access</strong> your personal data.</li><li>
          <strong>Rectify</strong> inaccurate or incomplete information.
        </li><li>
          <strong>Erase</strong> your personal data where legally applicable.
        </li><li>
          <strong>Restrict</strong> processing in certain circumstances.
        </li><li>
          <strong>Object</strong> to processing based on legitimate interests.
        </li><li><strong>Data portability</strong> where applicable.</li><li>
          <strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time where processing is based
          on consent.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>You may exercise these rights by contacting:</p>
      <p>
        <strong
          ><a href="mailto:victorandujarmurcia@gmail.com"
            >victorandujarmurcia@gmail.com</a
          ></strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        Please indicate that your request relates to data protection or privacy.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may request reasonable information to verify your identity where
        necessary before processing a request.
      </p>
      <h2>17. Right to Lodge a Complaint</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe that your personal data has been processed in violation
        of applicable data-protection legislation, you have the right to lodge a
        complaint with a competent supervisory authority.
      </p>
      <p>
        In Spain, the relevant authority is the <strong
          >Agencia Española de Protección de Datos (AEPD)</strong
        >.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may also contact Real Product first so that we have the opportunity
        to address your concern.
      </p>
      <h2>18. Security</h2>
      <p>
        Real Product takes reasonable technical and organisational measures
        appropriate to the nature of the information processed.
      </p>
      <p>
        However, no online service or method of electronic storage can guarantee
        absolute security.
      </p>
      <p>
        Users and clients should avoid transmitting credentials or highly
        sensitive information through channels not intended for that purpose.
      </p>
      <h2>19. Third-Party Websites</h2>
      <p>
        The Real Product website may link to third-party websites, repositories
        or services.
      </p>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy does not govern how those third parties process
        personal data. Their respective privacy policies apply when you interact
        with their services.
      </p>
      <h2>20. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy may be updated to reflect changes to the website,
        services, providers or applicable legal requirements.
      </p>
      <p>
        The latest version will be published on this website together with its
        date of revision.
      </p>
      <h2>21. Contact</h2>
      <p>For any privacy-related questions or requests:</p>
      <p>
        <strong>Víctor Andújar Murcia</strong><br /><strong>Real Product</strong
        ><br />Avinguda Comte Ramon Berenguer 146, Baixos 2a<br />08690 Santa
        Coloma de Cervelló, Barcelona, Spain<br /><strong
          ><a href="mailto:victorandujarmurcia@gmail.com"
            >victorandujarmurcia@gmail.com</a
          ></strong>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
